    <node id="scope_description:the_president_secretary_and_administrator_have_d:6798b76a31">
      <data key="d4">The President, Secretary, and Administrator have declared expanded use of AI is a national, departmental, and agency priority. The NA-1 NNSA Planning and Programming Guidance for Fiscal years 2028-2032 Future Years Nuclear Security Program (FYNSP) directs the establishment of a plan of record for the NNSA Genesis Mission, to include identifying funding requirements to accomplish the two sets of AI Genesis objectives (Platform and Mission S&amp;T Challenges (MiSTC)). In FY27, NA-11 submitted the UFR "Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence." The FY27 FYNSP UFR (which was accepted as a ROT) requested a total of $1,329,460K for all NA-11 program offices over the FYNSP. This new UFR represents a significant change from the previous year as early results from ASC's AI4NS sub-program projects now support the cost estimates and scope, and the Genesis Mission has officially been launched by the Department, marking a significant change in prioritization for the development of AI capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d5">scope_description</data>
      <data key="d6">combined_programming_data.csv</data>
    </node>
