    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_14">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">14</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML workflows and frontier-class AI models that use expanded underground test (UGT) diagnostic data and experimental datasets to reveal causal relationships in material response. This is fundamentally about exploiting and learning from rich historical and experimental nuclear data, aligning best with the challenge centered on digitizing, structuring, and leveraging America’s historic nuclear data and research. The other options emphasize real-time threat response or facility operations, which are not indicated in the scope description. Confidence is medium because the text does not explicitly mention digitization, but it clearly emphasizes AI models built on extensive nuclear test and experimental data. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">36412500.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_17">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">17</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on using machine learning to predict compatibility/incompatibility of energetic materials. This is directly aligned with AI-accelerated materials design, screening, and qualification workflows described in the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The work concerns material behavior and reliability for stockpile engineering (Aging &amp; Lifetimes), not nonproliferation monitoring or digitization of historical data, so the other two challenges are a poor fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">24666363.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_18">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">18</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description is “Materials Aging &amp; Compatibility,” and the WBS/STAT context is Aging &amp; Lifetimes within Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering. This aligns with work on understanding and qualifying materials behavior over time for the nuclear stockpile, which fits the challenge focused on accelerating materials discovery, production, and qualification for strategic deterrence. There is no indication of nonproliferation monitoring or historical data digitization, so the materials-focused challenge is the best match, though the description is brief, so confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">29440823.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_22">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">22</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on characterizing and validating energetic and shock mitigation materials to improve credibility of computational models, and on curating and analyzing new and legacy flight test data to predict environments of future systems. This is directly aligned with materials behavior, model validation, and test-data-driven prediction for future deterrence systems, which matches the materials discovery, production, and qualification lifecycle described in the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The other challenges center on historic nuclear data archives in general or nonproliferation monitoring, which do not fit the materials and delivery-environment emphasis here.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">22175000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_30">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">30</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on applying AI/ML techniques for qualification of CT data for part acceptance, which is directly about using AI to improve and streamline material/part qualification processes. This aligns with the Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification challenge, whose core aim is an AI-accelerated workflow for material/part qualification and reduced testing burden. The WBS and STAT context (Advanced Certification &amp; Qualification) further supports that this effort is about certification/qualification of components rather than enterprise-wide design–production integration or historical data digitization.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">1750000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_31">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">31</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on automated defect detection and machine learning models for additively manufactured (AM) metal components, which directly supports improving manufacturing reliability and qualification of mission-critical components. This aligns with the materials-focused challenge that emphasizes AI-driven workflows for material/part production, in-process anomaly detection, and qualification. The WBS and STAT context of advanced manufacturing development further supports a focus on production and qualification of components rather than enterprise-wide design/production integration or facility-level experimental throughput.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">5750000.0</data>
