      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request only state "Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence" without further detail. All three candidate challenges relate to deterrence and AI, so the mapping is ambiguous. As supporting context, the STAT L4 is Assessment Science and the WBS is Dynamic Materials Properties, which can align with nuclear material characterization and signatures more than with enterprise design/production integration or broad emergency response fusion. This slightly favors the attribution/signatures challenge, but the lack of specific forensic or response language keeps confidence low.</data>
