      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request emphasize “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence” within the STAT/WBS area of Secondary Assessment Technologies, which aligns more with nuclear forensics and characterization than with enterprise design/production integration or broad emergency response fusion. Among the options, the attribution-focused challenge centers on AI-enabled analysis of nuclear and radiological signatures to support deterrence, matching the assessment/forensics flavor implied by Secondary Assessment Technologies and the deterrence emphasis in the title. The evidence is brief and somewhat generic, so confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
