      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request both emphasize “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence” without further detail. The supporting STAT/WBS context is “Assessment Science” and specifically “Secondary Assessment Technologies,” which aligns most closely with nuclear material and radiological signature analysis rather than enterprise design/production integration or broad emergency response fusion. Among the candidate challenges, AI-enabled nuclear forensics and signature-based attribution (“Strengthening Deterrence Through Attribution of Nuclear and Radiological Signatures”) best matches secondary assessment and deterrence-focused AI tools, though the lack of explicit forensic language keeps confidence at medium.</data>
