      <data key="d17">The scope description is extremely short: “AI For Deterrence,” and the program request is “DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE,” which does not specify design/production integration or materials workflows. Among the three options, the only one whose core focus is directly on deterrence effects via AI, rather than on production or materials pipelines, is the attribution-focused challenge, which explicitly uses AI to strengthen nuclear deterrence. However, because the evidence is generic and could plausibly map to any deterrence-related AI effort, confidence is low.</data>
