      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request only state "Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence" with no further detail. All three candidate challenges relate to deterrence and AI, so the title alone is ambiguous. The WBS and STAT context (ICF Diagnostics &amp; Instrumentation under Inertial Confinement Fusion) suggest work on diagnostics and experimental support, which could align with either experimental capacity or nuclear-signature-related tools. Given the explicit emphasis on deterrence and nuclear context, and that attribution of nuclear and radiological signatures is directly tied to deterrence messaging, this row is most plausibly mapped to "Strengthening Deterrence Through Attribution of Nuclear and Radiological Signatures," but the lack of specific forensic or facility-operations language makes confidence low.</data>
