      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on productionizing AI tools that accelerate weapons design, modeling, and simulation workflows (CHANDLER federated model, Horizon Shield simulation workflow, CADSAT meshing tool) and deploying secure AI infrastructure on classified networks. These are generic AI/ASC-enabling capabilities rather than facility operations or DA/PA production integration. Among the three, they align best with the data- and simulation-ready pipeline emphasis in “Harnessing America’s Historic Nuclear Data and Research,” which explicitly calls for AI-driven meshing, simulation-ready datasets, and secure archival/compute environments. There is no mention of experimental facilities or DA/PA production handoff, so the other two challenges are less supported by the evidence. SME correction: Corrected</data>
