      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description ties this funding to NA-11’s mission and to the prior UFR titled “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence,” and the WBS/STAT context is Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support under Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering—both tightly aligned with weapons design, assessment, and production activities for deterrence. Among the Genesis challenges, those AI tools most directly map to integrating and accelerating nuclear weapons design and production operations rather than broad business/management processes or acquisition workflows, so the “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence” challenge is the best fit. Confidence is medium because the scope text is high-level and references the overall Genesis Mission rather than a specific challenge by name.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">30000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
