    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:15" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_15">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">15</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML work across multiple high energy density (HED) experiments, emphasizing analysis and modeling of experimental data to develop more refined approaches. This aligns most directly with the challenge centered on increasing experimental capacity and optimizing experiments at limited-capacity facilities, which explicitly targets AI-driven planning, execution, and analysis of experiments. The other challenges emphasize historical data digitization or design–production integration rather than improving ongoing experimental campaigns. The STAT/WBS context in Assessment Science and Secondary Assessment Technologies further supports a link to experimental design and analysis for stockpile stewardship.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">44130500.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
