    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:17" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_17">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">17</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on using machine learning to predict compatibility/incompatibility of energetic materials. This is directly aligned with AI-accelerated materials design, screening, and qualification workflows described in the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The work concerns material behavior and reliability for stockpile engineering (Aging &amp; Lifetimes), not nonproliferation monitoring or digitization of historical data, so the other two challenges are a poor fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">24666363.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
