    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:22" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_22">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">22</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on characterizing and validating energetic and shock mitigation materials to improve credibility of computational models, and on curating and analyzing new and legacy flight test data to predict environments of future systems. This is directly aligned with materials behavior, model validation, and test-data-driven prediction for future deterrence systems, which matches the materials discovery, production, and qualification lifecycle described in the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The other challenges center on historic nuclear data archives in general or nonproliferation monitoring, which do not fit the materials and delivery-environment emphasis here.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">22175000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
