    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:23" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_23">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">23</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on “novel physics modeling pertinent to reentry systems” with associated validation and uncertainty quantification. Reentry systems are directly tied to delivery environments for nuclear weapons and fall under Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering → Engineering → Delivery Environments, which aligns with design/engineering and production of deterrence systems rather than experimental facility operations or nuclear forensics. The emphasis on physics modeling and VUQ to support weapon delivery system performance and certification best matches the challenge centered on integrating design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, where multiscale physics models and uncertainty-aware methods are used to improve design–production alignment and modernization timelines.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">13900000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
