      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes NA-11’s prior UFR titled “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence” and frames this new UFR as a continuation and refinement of that effort under the Genesis Mission. Among the candidate challenges, only “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence” is explicitly centered on AI capabilities directly tied to nuclear deterrence design/production missions. The other two focus on business/management processes and acquisition, which are not mentioned in the scope. While the description is high-level and does not explicitly reference DA/PA integration or production twins, the clear nuclear deterrence AI focus and NA-11 stockpile R&amp;D context align best with the nuclear deterrence design/production challenge, justifying a medium confidence selection.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">33690000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
