      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">26</data>
      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on AI for ignition applications, double-shell experiments, simulations, analysis methods, and pulse-shaping machine learning in support of inertial confinement fusion and HED &amp; Ignition Science for stockpile applications. This is forward-looking, experiment- and simulation-centric AI, not digitization of historical records or materials discovery/qualification workflows. Among the three options, it aligns least poorly with the threat assessment/preparedness challenge, which emphasizes AI fusion of scientific data, simulations, and analysis for mission decision support, even though the match is indirect and not explicitly about emergency response. Hence the selection with low confidence. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">76113000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
