    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:29" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_29">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">29</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes NA-11’s role, nuclear deterrence, and development of AI capabilities supported by ASC’s AI4NS sub-program, which is tightly coupled to weapons design, stockpile stewardship, and related R&amp;D. The associated STAT/WBS context (Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering; Inertial Confinement Fusion; ICF Diagnostics &amp; Instrumentation) further anchors this funding to technical nuclear weapons design and experimental capabilities rather than business processes or acquisition workflows. Among the Genesis challenges, this aligns most directly with AI-enabled integration of design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, not with enterprise business management or acquisition modernization.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">5000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
