    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:31" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_31">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">31</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on automated defect detection and machine learning models for additively manufactured (AM) metal components, which directly supports improving manufacturing reliability and qualification of mission-critical components. This aligns with the materials-focused challenge that emphasizes AI-driven workflows for material/part production, in-process anomaly detection, and qualification. The WBS and STAT context of advanced manufacturing development further supports a focus on production and qualification of components rather than enterprise-wide design/production integration or facility-level experimental throughput.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">5750000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
