      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on developing a large language model to identify replacement HE binder candidates and on developing high‑performance, multi‑metal alloys optimized for strength and stability with new additive manufacturing methods to meet future system requirements. This is directly about discovering and developing new materials and manufacturing approaches for deterrence systems, which aligns with the materials discovery, production, and qualification lifecycle described in the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The emphasis is on materials R&amp;D and advanced manufacturing rather than DA/PA integration or experimental facility throughput, so the other two challenges are less aligned.</data>
