    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:34" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_34">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">34</data>
      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description is extremely terse: “Critical Executable CE UFR: Programmatic AI,” giving no direct indication of experiments, regulatory/safety documentation, or DA/PA integration. The WBS and STAT context place this in Multi-Weapon Systems under Stockpile Operations, which most closely aligns with enterprise-level, cross-cutting AI to support design–production integration and model-based systems engineering rather than facility experiment throughput or regulatory streamlining. Because the evidence is weak and largely inferential, confidence is low.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">165115000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA12</data>
    </edge>
