    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:35" target="mstc_challenge:strengthening_deterrence_through_attribution_of:12318fe125" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_35">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">35</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on significantly accelerating nuclear forensics attribution timelines after a nuclear or radiological incident, leveraging AI to improve post-event processing. This directly aligns with the attribution-centric nuclear forensics mission in “Strengthening Deterrence Through Attribution of Nuclear and Radiological Signatures,” which emphasizes AI-enabled nuclear forensics and rapid attribution of nuclear and radiological materials. The WBS/STAT labels of Forensics R&amp;D and the program request title “AI ACCELERATION FOR NUCLEAR FORENSICS TIMELINES” further support this mapping over the more general threat assessment/response or acquisition-focused challenges.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">150000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
