      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on accelerating AI for challenging proliferation detection scenarios, including AI-driven process modeling and system-of-systems digital twins, directly aligned with detecting and analyzing nuclear proliferation activities. This matches the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which emphasizes AI-enabled analysis of diverse data to detect proliferation-relevant anomalies. Supporting evidence includes the STAT lines for Proliferation Detection and the program request title “AI ACCELERATION FOR DETECTION OF FOREIGN PROLIFERATION,” both clearly oriented toward operational nonproliferation monitoring rather than archival data (Harnessing Historic Data) or AI policy/control concerns ((CUI) Preventing AI-Induced Nuclear Proliferation).</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">342000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
