    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:38" target="mstc_challenge:streamlining_production_removing_red_tape_and_en:5c22e0a6a3" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_38">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">38</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automation and AI/ML to enhance the e810 system and streamline the process for submitting civil nuclear technology transfer requests under 10 CFR Part 810. This is fundamentally an acquisition/authorization workflow and process-optimization problem—improving speed, efficiency, and consistency of a regulated approval pipeline—aligning best with the acquisition-focused challenge that emphasizes AI-enabled process automation and regulatory interpretation. While the work supports nonproliferation, the primary thrust is modernizing and accelerating a complex, regulation-driven enterprise process rather than building new detection/monitoring analytics or digitizing historic data, so it fits better under Accelerating Nuclear Enterprise Acquisition than the other two challenges. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
