    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:40" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_40">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">40</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on export control IT upgrades to accelerate technical reviews of export licenses for U.S. nuclear and dual-use commodities. This is directly tied to nonproliferation and control of nuclear-related materials and technologies, aligning with safeguarding against proliferation threats. Supporting evidence includes STAT and WBS labels (Nonproliferation and Arms Control, Nuclear Export Controls) and NA-20 context. While there is an element of process efficiency that could relate to acquisition, the core mission is export control for nonproliferation, making the safeguarding challenge the best fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">8000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA20</data>
    </edge>
