    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:41" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_41">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">41</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on designing and maintaining major reactor plant components and systems for technologically superior naval nuclear propulsion. This is fundamentally an engineering and production challenge—integrating design and production of complex nuclear systems—rather than an acquisition-process optimization or nonproliferation problem. Among the options, “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence” best matches work that improves the design–production pipeline for nuclear-related hardware, even though the text is specific to naval reactors rather than weapons. The other challenges center on acquisition efficiency or AI-induced proliferation, which are not reflected in the scope description.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">16200000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA30</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na30:23e20c395b" target="stat_l3:naval_reactors_programs:2d62a6a9af" id="has_stat_l3">
      <data key="d11">has_stat_l3</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">programming_data.csv</data>
      <data key="d14">41; 42</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na30:23e20c395b" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_41">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">41</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on designing and maintaining major reactor plant components and systems for technologically superior naval nuclear propulsion. This is fundamentally an engineering and production challenge—integrating design and production of complex nuclear systems—rather than an acquisition-process optimization or nonproliferation problem. Among the options, “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence” best matches work that improves the design–production pipeline for nuclear-related hardware, even though the text is specific to naval reactors rather than weapons. The other challenges center on acquisition efficiency or AI-induced proliferation, which are not reflected in the scope description.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">16200000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA30</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na30:23e20c395b" target="mstc_challenge:streamlining_production_removing_red_tape_and_en:5c22e0a6a3" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_42">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">42</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on ensuring Naval Reactors program operations meet or exceed applicable federal, state, and local standards and requirements, which is fundamentally about regulatory compliance, safety standards, and operational efficiency. This aligns directly with the challenge centered on streamlining production while maintaining rigorous safety and regulatory compliance in high-hazard facilities, rather than with design/production integration or materials discovery.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">5500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA30</data>
    </edge>
