    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:49" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_49">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">49</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope is to increase electrical import and distribution capacity to LANL, including new lines to the Supercomputing Center and between substations. This is mission-enabling infrastructure that directly supports higher experimental and computational throughput at a nuclear research site, aligning best with increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities. It does not focus on acquisition process optimization or materials discovery/qualification, so the acquisition and materials challenges are less applicable.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">115104000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
    </edge>
