    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:53" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_53">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">53</data>
      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description only indicates funding for a “New Central Computing Facility, Y-12 OPCs,” which is infrastructure for computing rather than clearly materials-focused or acquisition-focused work. Among the three options, expanded computing capacity most plausibly supports increased experimental and simulation throughput at a nuclear site, aligning best with the experimental capacity challenge, but the evidence is minimal and indirect, so confidence is low.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">3399000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA90</data>
