      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description, “HEA compositions for extreme environments,” points to research on high-entropy alloy behavior under extreme conditions, which most closely aligns with experimental materials science relevant to stockpile stewardship. The supporting STAT/WBS context (Assessment Science, Dynamic Materials Properties) suggests high-consequence experiments and materials characterization, which is more consistent with increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities than with nuclear threat response workflows or digitization of historical records. However, the mapping is indirect because the description does not explicitly mention facilities, experiments, or data archives, so confidence is low.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">1500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
