      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on a modular, data-driven ML approach for automatic calibration of Scorpius, a hydrodynamic/subcritical experimental capability used for stockpile assessment and certification. It explicitly references discrepancy learning techniques from NIF implosion design/control and certification methodologies, which aligns with AI-enabled, model-based systems engineering and calibration workflows that support nuclear weapons design, production, and certification. This is most consistent with the challenge on integrating design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, rather than business-process acceleration or digitization of historical archives.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">750000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
