      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope describes developing a modeling tool and digital twin to mirror the Scorpius experimental capability, integrated into the EPICS control system, combining multiple physics models and data sources (ITS data, PushML for accelerator gaps, beam transport codes, target dynamics, and radiography models). This aligns directly with the “facility operating system” and digital twin concepts in the Increasing Experimental Capacity challenge, which focuses on AI-enabled digital twins and integrated modeling to plan, steer, and analyze high-consequence experiments at limited-capacity facilities. It is not about digitizing historical records or enterprise business processes, so the other two challenges are a poor fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">3000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
