    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:17" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_17">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">17</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on machine learning work across multiple high energy density (HED) experiments, emphasizing analysis and modeling of experimental data and developing more refined uncertainty quantification (UQ) approaches. This aligns most closely with the experimental design, analysis, and throughput focus of “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities,” which centers on AI-driven facility operations, experiment steering, and uncertainty-aware analytics. The other challenges emphasize historical data digitization or design–production integration rather than improving real-time experimental data analysis and UQ for HED experiments.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">1500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
