    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:20" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_20">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">20</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on applying AI/ML to qualification of CT data for part acceptance and demonstrating digital twin performance with real data. This is directly about AI-enabled qualification workflows and validation of digital twins for parts, which aligns with accelerating materials and component qualification. The WBS and STAT context (Advanced Certification &amp; Qualification) further support a focus on material/component qualification rather than enterprise-wide design–production integration or historical data digitization, making the materials discovery/production/qualification challenge the best fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">4166000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
