    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:21" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_21">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">21</data>
      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description only states that CSSE works with Design Agencies on small-scale pilot projects to evaluate AI capabilities pursuant to the National Security Memorandum, without specifying business/management workflows or experimental facilities. Given the STAT/WBS context (Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering; Advanced Simulation and Computing; Computational Systems &amp; Software Environment) and collaboration with DAs on AI pilots, the most plausible alignment is with integrating AI into design/production workflows for nuclear deterrence, but the evidence is sparse and not explicit, so confidence is low.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">42491000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
