    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:26" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_26">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">26</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automated defect detection for additively manufactured (AM) structures and AI/ML for image interpretation to evaluate defect sizes and determine feasibility of using components for war reserve (WR) applications. This is directly about improving qualification and acceptance of manufactured components using AI, which aligns with the materials and manufacturing lifecycle and qualification focus of “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence.” The WBS and STAT context (“Weapon Technology and Manufacturing Maturation,” “Advanced Manufacturing Development”) further support a materials/manufacturing qualification challenge rather than historical data curation or enterprise-wide design/production integration.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">28300000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
