      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">True</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request both emphasize “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence,” but provide no detail on forensics or emergency response, making it unclear whether the focus is attribution, real‑time threat response, or weapons design/production. Given the STAT context (Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering; Assessment Science; Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support) and NA11’s role, the most plausible alignment is with AI tools that support weapons design, assessment, and production activities for deterrence, which best matches the design/production integration challenge rather than nuclear forensics or emergency response. The lack of explicit detail lowers confidence from high to medium.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">13576000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
