      <data key="d15">low</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request only state "Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence" without specifying whether the AI is for design/production integration, forensic attribution, or real-time emergency response. The STAT context (Assessment Science, Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support) leans toward stockpile assessment and experimental analysis rather than enterprise production workflows or fielded emergency response systems. Among the three, attribution of nuclear and radiological signatures most closely aligns with assessment-focused AI tools that support deterrence by characterizing and interpreting nuclear phenomena, but the evidence is very limited and non-specific, so confidence is low.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">33405000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
