      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description and program request both state “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence,” which is generic but clearly tied to deterrence and AI. Among the options, the first challenge is the only one explicitly centered on nuclear deterrence in a broad, enterprise/mission sense rather than facility throughput or forensic attribution. There is no mention of experiments, facilities, or forensics in the evidence, so the experimental-capacity and attribution challenges are less aligned. However, because the description does not explicitly reference design/production integration, the mapping is not definitive, leading to medium confidence.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">18467000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
