      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">44</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to revolutionize Defense Programs activities by accelerating design cycles, improving analysis of complex data sets, and reducing costs through efficiency. This aligns most directly with the design/production modernization and AI-accelerated, model-based engineering focus of “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence.” The program request title (“DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE”) and placement under Advanced Simulation and Computing further support a design-and-production oriented deterrence mission rather than archival data digitization or nuclear forensics attribution, though the evidence is somewhat general, so confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">52145000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
