    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:48" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_48">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">48</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI to revolutionize Defense Programs with accelerated design cycles, improved analysis of complex data, and reduced costs through efficiency. This aligns most directly with the design/production modernization and efficiency focus of “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which targets AI-accelerated, model-based engineering and production optimization. The other challenges focus on historical data digitization or nuclear forensics attribution, which are not indicated by the generic, enterprise-wide AI and design-cycle language in the scope. Supporting context from STAT/WBS (Advanced Simulation and Computing, Integrated Codes) also fits better with AI-enabled design and production modeling than with archival digitization or forensic attribution.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">65092000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
