      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data sets, and reduce costs across Defense Programs, which aligns most directly with integrating and modernizing design and production workflows for nuclear deterrence. The program request explicitly focuses on developing AI tools for nuclear deterrence, and the STAT/WBS context (Advanced Simulation and Computing, Integrated Codes) supports an AI- and modeling-centric effort tied to weapons design and production rather than archival data digitization or regulatory/safety process optimization. Therefore, it best maps to “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence.”</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">54157000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
