      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to revolutionize Defense Programs with accelerated design cycles, improved analysis of complex data, and reduced costs through efficiency. Combined with the program request, “DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE,” and the STAT/WBS focus on Physics &amp; Engineering Models under Advanced Simulation and Computing, this aligns best with the challenge centered on AI-accelerated, model-based systems engineering that integrates design and production for nuclear deterrence. The other challenges focus on historical data digitization or experimental facility throughput rather than design/production integration and deterrence-focused AI tools.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">13036000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
    </edge>
