      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data sets, and reduce costs across Defense Programs. Combined with the program request “DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE” and placement under Advanced Simulation and Computing / Verification and Validation, this aligns best with the challenge focused on AI-accelerated, model-based systems engineering that integrates design and production for nuclear deterrence. While there is some overlap with broader efficiency and safety themes, the explicit focus on design cycles and deterrence points more directly to “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence.”</data>
