    <edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:53" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_53">
      <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">53</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data sets, and reduce costs across Defense Programs, which aligns most directly with integrating design and production workflows for nuclear deterrence. The program request explicitly focuses on developing AI tools for nuclear deterrence, matching the deterrence-focused, design/production modernization theme of the Integrating Design and Production Operations challenge more than the archival/data-preservation or regulatory/safety-streamlining emphases of the other two options. However, the description is broad and not explicitly about DA/PA handoff, so confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
      <data key="d18">ROT</data>
      <data key="d19">15642000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA11</data>
