    <edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:strengthening_deterrence_through_attribution_of:12318fe125" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_46">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">46</data>
      <data key="d15">medium</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes “surge support for advancing AI-tools for rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events that require detailed analysis of vast and varied data,” which closely matches the Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response challenge language about rapid response to nuclear/radiological events, real-time situational awareness, and multimodal data fusion. While the description also mentions improving the speed and accuracy of nuclear forensics analyses (which aligns with the Attribution challenge), the primary focus and first-listed objective is rapid response to events using AI over varied data streams, so the response-focused challenge is the best overall fit. SME correction: Corrected</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="leads_challenge">
      <data key="d11">leads_challenge</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">ProgramOffice_Mapping.csv</data>
      <data key="d14">8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_44">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">44</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes “rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events,” “detailed analysis of vast and varied data,” and generally improving nuclear risk mitigation and response. These align directly with the challenge focused on accelerating nuclear threat assessment, preparedness, and response via multimodal AI fusion for real-time decision support. While it also mentions improving nuclear forensics, the dominant thrust is event response and preparedness rather than primary attribution, so the first challenge is the best fit.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">5000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_47">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">47</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes “rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events,” “detailed analysis of vast and varied data,” and generally improving response capabilities, which directly matches the problem statement and proposed solution for the Accelerating Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response challenge. While it also mentions improving the speed and accuracy of nuclear forensics, the dominant focus is on real-time event response and risk mitigation, aligning more with NEST-style emergency support than with dedicated attribution/forensics or historic data efforts. The WBS and STAT context (Nuclear Incident Response/NEST) further support this mapping.</data>
      <data key="d18">UFR</data>
      <data key="d19">87500000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_31">
      <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
      <data key="d14">31</data>
      <data key="d15">high</data>
      <data key="d16">False</data>
      <data key="d17">The scope focuses on analyzing nuclear materials and device designs to advise and enable an effective U.S. Government response to the potential use of a nuclear threat device. This aligns directly with rapid threat assessment and response to nuclear/radiological events, matching the mission of “Accelerating Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response.” The WBS and STAT context (Nuclear Counterterrorism and Incident Response, Nuclear Threat Science) further support an emergency response and threat assessment focus rather than long-term nonproliferation monitoring or AI-induced proliferation concerns.</data>
      <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
      <data key="d19">75000000.0</data>
      <data key="d20">NA80</data>
    </edge>
